GUR, Ⅵ. (P.) Ā. guráte: simple verb 🞄only in pp. gūrtá, welcome, pleasing. 🞄apa, disapprove;
 threaten. ava, threaten, 🞄assault (d., lc.): gd. -gūrya. ā, approve, assent 🞄to (ac.);
 pronounce the āgur. ud, pp. 🞄-gūrṇa, raised threateningly;
 lifted up.

gur-ú, a. (v-ī) heavy;
 heavier than (ab.);
 🞄great, large;
 violent, serious, hard, severe;
 🞄weary, sad (days);
 important, weighty, of much 🞄account;
 venerable;
 prosodically long;
 m. 🞄venerable or highly respected person: father, 🞄mother, or elder relative, esp. teacher: du. 🞄parents;
 pl. parents and other venerable persons, 🞄also teacher (pl. of respect);
 chief of (g. 🞄pl. or —˚).

guru-karman, n. affair of the 🞄teacher;
 -kārya, n. important business;
 -kula, 🞄n. teacherʼs house: -vāsa, m. sojourn in a 🞄teacherʼs house, tutelary stage in a Brāhmanʼs 🞄life;
 -kṛta, pp. made much of, lauded;
 🞄-kratu, m. great sacrifice;
 -gṛha, n. preceptorʼs 🞄house;
 -jana, m. venerable person, 🞄father, mother, parents;
 -talpa, m. teacherʼs 🞄conjugal bed;
 violation of oneʼs preceptorʼs 🞄bed: -ga, -gāmin, a. defiling a teacherʼs 🞄conjugal bed, -abhigamana, n. violation 🞄of oneʼs teacherʼs bed;
 -talpin, a. = talpaga;
 🞄-tā, f. heaviness;
 importance;
 dignity;
 🞄condition of a teacher;
 -tva, n. id.;
 prosodical 🞄length: -ka, n. heaviness;
 -darśana, 🞄n. sight of oneʼs teacher;
 -dāra, m. teacherʼs 🞄wife;
 -dhur, f. pl. severe task;
 -patnī, f. 🞄teacherʼs wife;
 -pūjā, f. reverence towards 🞄a teacher;
 -prasādanīya, fp. obliging to oneʼs 🞄teacher;
 -prasūta, pp. permitted or bidden 🞄by elder relatives;
 -bhāryā, f. teacherʼs wife.

guru-laghu-tā, f. great and little 🞄value;
 -lāghava, n. importance and insignificance, 🞄relative value;
 -loka, m. powerful 🞄men;
 -vat, ad. like a preceptor (= nm. or lc.);
 🞄-vāsa, m. sojourn with a preceptor, pupilage;
 🞄-vṛtti, f. (proper) behaviour towards oneʼs 🞄teacher: -para, a. intent on oneʼs teacher;
 🞄-śuśrūṣā, f. obedience towards oneʼs teacher;
 🞄-śuśrūṣu, a. obedient to oneʼs teacher;
 -sakhī, f. female friend of an elder relative;
 🞄-saṃnidhi, m. presence of the teacher;
 -samavāya, m. plurality of teachers;
 -strī-gamanīya, fp. relating to adultery with a teacherʼs 🞄wife.

guru‿artha, 〈1.〉 m. important matter;
 🞄affair concerning oneʼs teacher;
 preceptorʼs 🞄fee: -m, ad. for oneʼs parents or teacher;
 🞄〈2.〉 a. begging for oneʼs teacher.
